## Interface: 16001
## Title: |cffC9A24ATwich|rUI Fishing
## Notes: One key that fishes for you to press: equips your pole, applies a lure, casts, reels in and opens the clams you catch, each on your own key press. Keeps a record of your fishing sessions and catches. Loaded when you bind its key or type /tui fish; keep it turned on alongside TwichUI.
## Author: twichie
## Version: 1.0.0
## RequiredDeps: !!!TwichUI
## LoadOnDemand: 1
## SavedVariables: TwichUIFishingDB
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\!!!TwichUI\media\icon
## X-License: MIT (code); see !!!TwichUI\LICENSE
## Category: Interface Enhancements

# Names, seed data and small helpers (no frames, no game state); creates R.Fishing
Data.lua
# TwichUIFishingDB: schema, defaults, migrations and retention (docs/fishing.md, "Saved data")
Store.lua
# Fishing sessions, casts and lifetime totals
Session.lua
# The fishing pole, the optional outfit, and putting your own gear back
Gear.lua
# Fishing lures on the pole: what is on it, what is in the bags, which to use
Lure.lua
# Clams and other containers caught while fishing: the queue, opening and what they held
Containers.lua
# Loot windows: catches and the items taken from them
Loot.lua
# The fishing key: the next action, the secure buttons, reeling and combat
Action.lua
# The read-only interface later stages use, and the diagnostics
Api.lua
# Start-up, events and /tui fish
Main.lua
# Stage 2, Fishing Mode: what the heads-up pieces share (artwork in media\, built by tools/make_fishing_art.py)
Hud.lua
# The Fishing Mode camera, put back as it was afterwards
Camera.lua
# Fading the interface around Fishing Mode, and bringing it back
Fade.lua
# The fishing cast bar
CastBar.lua
# The catch list on the right of the screen
CatchList.lua
# Catch notifications
Toast.lua
# Fishing Mode itself: presentations, on and off, recovery, and its /tui fish words
Present.lua
